🧾 Supplier Evaluation Macro – Simple Explanation for Meeting

1. Purpose of the Macro

“The purpose of this macro is to automatically consolidate and update the Supplier Evaluation Summary file.
It reduces manual work and prevents encoding errors.”


---

2. How the Process Works

The system reads all supplier evaluation files from the assigned folder.

It checks if the required sheet and data are complete.

It validates the material type (Direct or Indirect).

If the file is correct:

Data is transferred to the Summary sheet.

The file is moved to the Completed folder.


If there is an error:

The file is moved to the Invalid folder.

The error details are recorded in the Error Log sheet.




---

3. Error Handling

“If there is an issue such as missing sheet name, wrong material type, or archive error,
the system will:

Show an error message

Record the error in the Error Log sheet

Include:

Timestamp

Supplier Code

Last Archive Source

Error Description

Remarks”



This helps us monitor and trace issues easily.


---

4. Improvements Made

Added dedicated Invalid folder handling

Added detailed Error Log sheet

Separated archive errors from validation errors

Improved traceability using Supplier Code and timestamp



---

5. Benefits

Faster processing

Less manual checking

Better monitoring of invalid files

More accurate supplier evaluation summary



